.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt TIME.CONF 5
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm time.conf
.Nd explicit boot-local unauthenticated SNTP policy for the existing NIC owner
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/time.conf
is read by sshd at startup. A missing file disables synchronization. Changing
it requires restarting sshd; no silent live activation occurs.
Sessions do not acquire a writable /etc view. Supply time.conf through the
existing image builder --etc directory or its offline reconfigure path; the
file is not activated live.
.Pp
Use one keyword and value per line; blank lines and lines beginning with
# are ignored. Only printable ASCII, spaces, tabs and newlines are accepted.
Unknown/duplicate keywords, extra words, invalid values and files over 4096
bytes prevent remote SSH startup rather than silently replacing operator policy.
An enrolled local shell remains available when FSD and enrollment are usable;
otherwise init can retain read-only kernel maintenance. Preserve the startup
console and stop the exact owned launcher before repairing this startup-only
file through the image builder's offline reconfigure path, then restart.
Neither local path activates this file live.
.Bl -tag -width max-step-seconds
.It Cm enabled yes Ns | Ns Cm no
Default no. No outgoing query occurs unless enabled and an explicit server is
configured.
.It Cm server Ar IPv4
One unicast dotted IPv4 peer, required when enabled. No DNS, multicast,
broadcast or public default server is used.
.It Cm server-port Ar port
Exact UDP peer port, 1..65535; default 123. A nonprivileged private test peer can
use a high port without altering its host clock.
.It Cm local-port Ar port
Exclusive local UDP port, 1024..65535; default 49123. An occupied port refuses the
attempt; another service's endpoint is never taken. The native stack also
refuses loopback, local/subnet/broadcast destinations and off-subnet peers
without a configured route.
.It Cm interval-seconds Ar seconds
Normal refresh/refusal interval 60..86400; default 3600. With the link up,
timeouts pause 1, 2, 4 seconds and double up to this interval. KoD, stratum
refusal and other non-timeout failures wait the normal interval. A down link
waits for carrier without periodic queries or failure records; a link-waiting
provider re-arms on carrier rise. Success resets timeout backoff. Retry-state
changes are logged once, with bounded summaries. A manual assertion retains
its automatic-work cancellation and waits the configured interval.
.It Cm max-step-seconds Ar seconds
Maximum absolute difference from known current civil time, 1..315360000;
default 86400. A larger disagreement is refused and retains the prior clock.
Unknown time may bootstrap from the configured estimate, and the first network
sample can replace an eligible RTC anchor without this bound. RTC readings
before the fixed 2026 build floor are unknown. The limit applies to later
network corrections relative to a prior network sample or operator assertion,
with no cumulative bound. Explicit authenticated operator assertions themselves
are not step-bounded and remain supported throughout 1970..2099.
A manual assertion is replaced by the next successful periodic estimate within
this limit. A larger difference retains the assertion and records error -34
on each attempted interval until the assertion or provider policy changes.
.It Cm max-age-seconds Ar seconds
Successful network sample age 60..86400, at least the retry interval;
default 21600. An older estimate is marked stale and continues advancing until
replaced. Age uses delivered monotonic ticks, not a proven external elapsed
or suspend-aware clock.
.El
.Pp
Each query uses at most 3 nonce-correlated requests, 2 seconds per attempt and
8 seconds total in boot time, driven nonblockingly inside the existing owner
loop. Malformed/late responses, entropy or transport failure and step-policy
refusal retire the attempt. Last successful source/value and latest failure
remain separately observable with
.Nm date Fl -status .
.Pp
The existing SNTP parser's explicit 2026..2035 era window is retained. Server
transmit time is an unauthenticated estimate anchored at local receipt; RTT is
only a transport observation. It is not an authenticated UTC error bound, and
no symmetric-delay accuracy claim is made. All corrections are software-only,
boot-local and do not feed TLS trust or write the RTC. Monotonic timeouts, RT
budgets and watchdogs are independent.
.Sh EXAMPLES
An explicitly selected private test peer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
enabled yes
server 10.0.2.2
server-port 40123
interval-seconds 3600
max-step-seconds 86400
max-age-seconds 21600
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clock 1 ,
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr network.conf 5 ,
.Xr afterboot 8
